      "writtenOn": "2020-04-06T22:30:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s still standard on Debian-based distros, but not created by default on Gentoo or Arch, it seems.  I\u0027m not sure if any group has replaced plugdev as the common way of providing access to these sorts of devices; AFAIKT the group just gets created as necessary on platforms where it doesn\u0027t exist by default.\n\nvapier@ probably has an opinion, but we could (1) not install the udev rule if plugdev doesn\u0027t exist, (2) create plugdev as a system group if it doesn\u0027t exist, or (3) install the udev rule anyway and let it fail",
      "parentUuid": "c4d26c26_a0e8a59c",
